      "challengedBy": [],
      "claim": "In the credential-sync branch, refreshOAuthTokens returns the raw fetch Response (line 15), but changed consumers such as GoogleCalendarService still expect a parsed object and immediately read res?.data and token.access_token from the return value. When CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED is on and CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_ENDPOINT is set, refreshAccessToken will receive a Response without a data field, so access_token/expiryDate updates can fail or write undefined values.",
