    {
      "challengedBy": [],
      "claim": "When `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` and `CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_ENDPOINT` are set, `refreshOAuthTokens` returns the raw `fetch()` `Response` object (`return response;`) rather than the JSON token payload that downstream code expects. Changed consumers such as `packages/app-store/googlecalendar/lib/CalendarService.ts` and `packages/app-store/hubspot/lib/CalendarService.ts` call `refreshOAuthTokens(...)` and then pass the result into `parseRefreshTokenResponse(...)`/token handling logic that reads fields like `access_token`, `refresh_token`, and expiry fields. A `Response` object does not have those fields, so the refresh path will fail at runtime with invalid token parsing or missing-field errors whenever credential sync is enabled.",
      "confidence": 0.7200000286102295,
      "discoveredBy": [
        "unit-008",
        "unit-010"
      ],
